-- title:
--   Completion of a DVR as O[[X]]/(X-varpi)
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and let $\varpi \in O$ be an irreducible element. Write $\mathfrak m = \mathrm{IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal}\ O$ for the maximal ideal of $O$, and let $\widehat{O} = \mathrm{AdicCompletion}\ \mathfrak m\ O$ be the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $O$, regarded as an $O$-algebra. Consider the ideal of the power series ring $O[[X]]$ generated by the single element $X - C(\varpi)$, where $C$ is the inclusion of constants. The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism
--   $$e \colon \widehat{O} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; O[[X]]/\bigl(X - C(\varpi)\bigr)$$
--   (an equivalence respecting both addition and multiplication) such that for every $o \in O$ the image under $e$ of the canonical image of $o$ in $\widehat{O}$ is the class of the constant power series $C(o)$. Thus $e$ is an isomorphism of $O$-algebras, and in particular it matches the canonical map $O \to \widehat{O}$ with the map $o \mapsto \overline{C(o)}$; applied to $o = \varpi$ it sends the image of $\varpi$ to the class of $X$.
--
--   This is the classical description of a complete discrete valuation ring by $\varpi$-adic expansions, in the form $\widehat{O} \cong O[[X]]/(X-\varpi)$, together with the compatibility on constants that makes the isomorphism $O$-linear. It is the companion of [`PowerSeries.isAdicComplete_quotient_span_X_sub_C_of_irreducible`](thm.html#PowerSeries.isAdicComplete_quotient_span_X_sub_C_of_irreducible), which supplies the domain, discrete valuation ring and adic completeness structure on the quotient and the irreducibility of the class of $\varpi$ there, and it is used in the construction of local crossing models of modular curves and in the coefficient rigidity statements for prolongation tuples.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PowerSeries_exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_span_X_sub_C.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
